I'm not sure whether anyone noticed but the Kops are complete wimps.  With
my chaotic Barbarian, I usually pick up all the non-breakable valuable items
in a shop and apply the pick-axe/kicking trick.  After transferring all the
gold from the shopkeeper's pocket to my, I have enough money to buy the
breakable items i want.  I then throw a completely worthless item (e.g.
a worthless piece of glass) from outside the shop and retrieve it, now in
debt of a mere seven gold pieces.  Existing through the passage I made, I whop
all the Kops as they come to me and safely rack up massive experience points
and a overwhelming supply of cream pies.  I always eat a floating eye corpse
before attempting this, of course, to avoid complete blindness.  If the
shopkeeper happened to come after me (half of the time he/she didn't), I only
need to pay up the few coins and no further grudge would be held.  If the
shopkeeper stayed in the store, I just wipe out the squads of Kops and return
to pay for the item.  Repeating the process is slow and boring as heck but I
keep getting killed in the lower levels if I don't get my character up to
twelfth level first.  I would appreciate any comments on my current tactic
or how prudent should I be descending the dungeon.


